docs/ holds US government public records (the SEC order) and USPTO patent documents; the MIT License does not cover them:
- docs/sec_order_2017_33-10280.pdf and docs/sec_order_2017_33-10280.txt: In the Matter of Citadel Securities LLC,
  Securities Act Release No. 10280, January 13, 2017, an order of the US Securities and Exchange Commission
  (https://www.sec.gov/litigation/admin/2017/33-10280.pdf).
- docs/patents/: US 7,587,347 B2 and US 7,987,128 B2 as published by the United States Patent and Trademark Office.
- docs/img/sec_*.png, docs/img/patent_front.png and docs/img/sec_collage.png: figures that show pages and excerpts of
  those documents (the page images they are built from are in docs/img/src/pages/ and docs/img/src/figures/assets/;
  docs/img/social_preview.png also shows crops of the SEC order). The other figures in docs/img/ are this project's
  own (MIT).

docs/img/src/figures/fonts/ holds the Inter and JetBrains Mono fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL.txt in
that folder).

This project rebuilds, from those public documents, rules that the SEC order describes. It is not Citadel's code and
is not affiliated with Citadel Securities LLC or Citadel Investment Group.
